3.34  2026-08-23

    - TKT-393. TKT-386 fixed the TOON encoder for a map nested inside a
      list item, but Data::TOON's decoder could not read that shape
      back even once it was written correctly - a different gap,
      established with well-formed input. Its list-item parser only
      recursed into a nested map when it was the item's FIRST key;
      every later key was parsed as a primitive unconditionally, so an
      empty value there (a nested map's own line) became the empty
      string and the parser then stopped at that map's own indented
      lines, dropping every field after it too - including when the
      nested map itself was the first key, a second manifestation of
      the same defect found while testing.

    - Fixed: Data::TOON::Decoder::_decode_array_value now applies the
      same empty-means-nested-object rule _decode_object already has,
      to every key in a list item. No internal caller is affected -
      Tira decodes TOON in one test only, guarding a scalar - but
      anyone piping Tira's default output through a TOON decoder no
      longer loses data silently.

