      now asserted on both forms.

2.31  2026-08-16

    - TKT-221: --column-role can be given. The command reference offered it
      beside --enter-role and --before-role; it was never in the parser, so
      policy.add answered "Unknown option: column-role" and refused the
      whole command, while the engine declared the field and stored it.
    - And no rule read it. The field was storable, documented and evaluated
      in the loop that saves a policy, but only enter and before were ever
      resolved through a role - so a policy declared by column role would
      have watched a column called nothing. Every rule that watches a
      column now resolves it the same way: card-duration, checklist-idle,
      wip-limit and gate-missing.
    - Why 100% coverage did not catch it, which is the more useful half.
      The loop that stores the three roles has all its statements executed
      by the tests that set the other two; the pass for this one reaches a
      covered "next if !defined" and stops. A field can be declared,
      evaluated, documented and fully covered and still have never once
      held a value. Coverage says a line ran, not that a case was tried.
    - Three lines that copied the role fields into the policy are gone.
      They arrive in the arguments every command passes through and
      policy_add reads them from there - proved by taking one away and
      watching nothing change, which is what made it worth removing.

