      log-only appeared on his terminal exactly like one set to
      bridge-reminder, and print-reminder did nothing log-only did not.
      Found by the hourly bug hunt.
    - The policies guide states it as a table: print-reminder goes to the
      owner's police terminal, log-only is recorded and said to nobody,
      for when you are tuning a rule and do not want the noise yet. The
      second row was not true, and it was untrue in exactly the situation
      it exists for - you reach for log-only to stop the noise and it put
      the rule on his terminal anyway.
    - Escalation decides when the owner is told; the action now decides
      whether. A log-only violation is still recorded, because a rule you
