0.83  2026-08-09
    - A card with a question nobody has answered is no longer chased.
      While it waits it is in the owner's hands, not the agent's, and
      chasing the agent for it is the fastest way to teach an agent
      that the reminders are noise.
    - When the last question is answered the clock starts from the
      answer rather than the move, so answering after three days does
      not make the card instantly overdue and blame the agent for the
      delay. Escalation restarts at level one, because the agent was
      blocked rather than idle.
    - An all-clear tells the agent every question on the card is
      answered and it is back with them. It is owed once per round of
      questions, and both it and the level are derived by counting
      rows rather than stored, so there is no flag to fall out of step.
    - None of this waits on the agent marking the answers: that is its
      own business, and waiting for it would let an agent dodge the
      reminders forever by never marking anything.
    - Notification databases written before this release are migrated
      in place rather than started again.

0.82  2026-08-09
    - A card waiting on somebody is drawn yellow, in either direction: a
      question nobody has answered waits on the owner, an answer nobody
      has read and marked waits on the agent. It returns to its ordinary
      colour only once every question is settled. Reading an answer is
      not the same as agreeing with it, so a read-but-unmarked answer
      still shows as waiting.
    - Knowing this means opening the card, so the flag is computed
      wherever the card is read anyway. The ref-only dashboard still
      opens nothing and is as cheap as it always was. While here, the
